</div></div></div><div class="fe-block fe-block-a8d91848ee639fad4dda"><div class="sqs-block website-component-block sqs-block-website-component sqs-block-html html-block" data-block-css="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.[long].components.[long].components.html.styles.css&quot;]" data-block-scripts="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.[long].components.[long].components.html.visitor.js&quot;]" data-block-type="1337" data-definition-name="website.components.html" data-sqsp-block="text" data-website-component-id="a8d91848ee639fad4dda" id="block-a8d91848ee639fad4dda"><div class="sqs-block-content"><div class="sqs-text-block-container">
  
  <div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The Heart of Maryland Bowhunters (HMB) was established in 1994 as a place for a small group of bowhunters to get together to practice their archery skills.  Over the past 30 years we have grown into one of the very best 3D archery courses in Maryland. </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The club is situated on 40 acres of the Patapsco State Park with three dedicated members-only practice ranges and a 3/4 mile loop course with 30 3D targets.  The three practice ranges consist of a range with nine target butts placed at distances between 10 to 65 yards on a flat range, an elevated shooting platform (normally with at least six 3D targets), and a walk-through 3D range with 20 targets ranging in distances from 15 to 60 yards.  The three practice ranges are available to all members at any time of the year, while the 30-target 3D course is reserved for when we have shoots that are open to the public. </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">  </p></div>


  








